Z||000006||Cooter||12-29-2000||08:25 PM||||Those early F body dashes were neat. If you have never seen one, they were really ahead of their time. They were supposed to have been used in the 82's, but they were not very durable so production was delayed for a couple of years until better designs and materials were available. By today's standards, they are very "eightyish". The stereo was on a "pod" that could be turned to face the driver or passenger. The turn signal switch was integrated into the dash and was not a part of the column-kind of like an Impulse of the same era. It would be an interesting add on in a Fiero, but if it ever quit working you might not ever find another one.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tweek||12-29-2000||11:03 PM||||Well, Eightyish is good!! After all they are the same year, which hopefully might help make is possible, I'll look into it more and keep ya'll posted on what happens. Course I dont have a garage so it may be something for Spring I suppose. Cheers!<P>-Ted||||reg||1
